- Risk: runway under 9 months if we maintain status quo
- Opportunity: 2 high-impact levers (COGS improvement + Opex reduction) can extend runway to ~14 months with limited revenue growth sacrifice

Slide 3 — Plan (30/60/90)
- 30d: hiring freeze, supplier renegotiations, pricing changes pilot, freeze discretionary spend
- 60d: implement procurement changes, product rationalization, sales channel re-allocation
- 90d: operational improvements, begin automation projects, evaluate productizing recurring revenue

Slide 4 — Expected outcomes & asks
- Scenario chart (runway vs. net monthly burn)
- KPI targets (gross margin +5 ppt, Opex -20% → runway ~14 months)
- Asks for leadership: approve 30d measures, target department cuts, provide list of nonnegotiables

8) Risks and governance
- Be explicit about customer and revenue risk from aggressive cuts (e.g., cutting S&M may slow growth). Attach contingency plan and assign owners for each cut.
- Monthly board reporting: update burn, cash, revenue, gross margin, top 5 cost actions and status.

9) What I can do next (pick one)
