  2) Cost discipline (0–60 days): hiring freeze, cut discretionary OpEx, renegotiate contracts.  
  3) Working capital (30–120 days): shorten DSO and extend DPO; consider receivables financing if necessary.  
  4) Scale plan (90–360 days): evaluate automation vs. contract manufacturing with ROI analysis; ramp high‑margin product lines and services.
- Expected impact & ask: “Conservative execution of these measures can reduce net burn by ~$80–120k/month and improve gross margin by several points, which would extend runway materially (to the ~14 month target) and put us on a path to positive operating cashflow within X quarters. Ask: approval to implement hiring freeze, prioritize supplier renegotiation, and allocate up to $X for a yield improvement project.” (I will tailor X once you give the P&L.)

D. Suggested slides / one‑pager structure
1) Snapshot: cash, runway (show different calculations), last quarter revenue, monthly revenue.
2) Problem statement: margin breakdown by product / COGS drivers + OpEx drivers.
3) 90‑day plan (specific actions + owners + expected $/month impact).
4) 6–12 month scale plan (automation/outsource decision framework + capex and ROI).
5) Sensitivity table: runway under Base / Actions / Stretch.
6) Ask and decision points.

E. KPIs to include in your materials
