  - If needed, prepare a short capital raise plan (bridge or extension) only after exhausting cost & margin levers.

Margin-improvement levers (practical examples)
- Gross margin:
  - Negotiate input prices, consolidate suppliers, switch to lower-cost materials with equivalent specs.
  - Reengineer BOM to reduce parts cost / improve yields.
  - Shift product mix toward higher-margin SKUs; sunset low-margin items.
  - Increase average selling price where the market permits by packaging value or reducing discounting.

