Medium-term (3–9 months) — structural improvement
- COGS optimization: supplier consolidation, negotiate BOM/part changes, offshore/nearshore production where feasible.
- Product redesign for manufacturability: simplify designs, reduce component count.
- Move fixed costs to variable: outsource non-core functions, use contractors/partners for scaling.
- Margin-focused go-to-market: change commissions/comp plans to favor profitable deals, emphasize upsell/cross-sell.
- Improve collections & cash conversion: tighten AR processes, incentivize faster payments.

Long-term (9–18 months) — scalable growth
- Platform/automation investments: automate core ops to reduce headcount per $ revenue as you scale.
- Subscription or recurring revenue models: increase predictability and LTV.
- Enter higher-margin adjacent markets or channels: value-add services, licensing, aftermarket parts.
- Strategic partnerships & distribution channels: scale sales without proportional SG&A increases.

Concrete KPI targets to measure and present
- Gross margin (%)
- Net cash burn ($/month)
- Runway (months)
- Revenue run-rate (MRR or equivalent)
- CAC, LTV, LTV:CAC
- Contribution margin per product/customer
