Plan and targets: “Over the next 90 days we will implement targeted price increases, SKU rationalization, supplier renegotiations, and working capital improvements to immediately reduce net burn. Medium-term (3–9 months) we will drive factory yield, implement design-for-cost changes, and shift sales toward higher-margin accounts. Our goal is to reduce net burn by $90K/month (or improve combined margin and cost structure by ~37%) to reach an internal runway target of ~14 months while simultaneously enabling 15–25% revenue growth over the next 12 months. We will report progress through a weekly cash KPI and a monthly board pack that tracks runway, gross margin, DSO, inventory turns and contribution margin by product line.”

E — Slide/deck outline (recommended 6–8 slides)
1. Executive summary (1 slide): cash, runway, revenue, ask/decision required
2. Current operating P&L snapshot (1 slide): Revenue, COGS, Gross margin, SG&A, Net burn
3. Runway sensitivity (1 slide): Base, downside, upside with simple table/charts
4. Initiatives & expected impact (1–2 slides): quick wins, medium and long term, owners, timing, expected $/month impact
5. KPI dashboard & cadence (1 slide): what will be tracked and frequency
6. Risks & mitigations (1 slide): supplier risk, demand risk, timing risk
7. Ask / next steps (1 slide): approvals, hires/freeze, vendor negotiation authority, modeling tasks

F — Example estimated impact (to include in materials)
- Quick wins (0–90 days): price +3% => +$24K gross/month; supplier savings and DSO => +$30–$50K/month cash effect combined.
- Ops improvements (3–9 months): 5–10pp gross margin improvement => +$40–$80K/month on current revenue.
- Combined aim = $90K+/month improvement to hit 14 months runway (mix of margin lift and cost cuts).

Next steps I can take for you (pick one):
