- Supplier renegotiation: lower material costs, longer payment terms, volume discounts, dual sourcing.
- Reduce discretionary spend: hiring freeze (non-critical roles), marketing reallocation to highest-ROI channels.
- Working capital fixes: reduce DSO, accelerate collections, tighten credit, reduce inventory buffers.

Medium-term (3–9 months)
- Design for cost: redesign products/components for fewer parts, cheaper sub-suppliers, standardization that reduces per-unit cost.
- Manufacturing efficiency: reduce scrap/yield losses, lean manufacturing, setup-time reduction to increase capacity utilization.
