- Week 2–8: Vendor and freight renegotiations (Procurement). KPI: signed savings targets (e.g., $30k/mo).
- Week 3–12: Manufacturing efficiency blitz (Plant Ops + Continuous Improvement) — run 5S/OEE projects on a pilot line. KPI: OEE + scrap reduction; estimated $/month savings.
- Week 4–12: Revenue quick wins (Sales) — targeted price tests, focus on top 20% customers and top SKUs. KPI: incremental revenue / GM% lift.
- Ongoing: build a 12‑month rolling cash model and weekly cash dashboard (Finance). KPI: weekly cash balance, burn, committed cash needs.

5) Finance narrative (short version you can read out in 90 seconds)
- Current state: “Metro Manufacturing has $2.1M in cash today, revenue run‑rate of ~$2.4M/quarter ($800k/month), and a reported net burn of ~$240k/month. Our current cash position supports roughly 9 months at the present burn — we need to reconcile the 14‑month number and take action.”
- Goal: “Deliver a 14‑month runway while protecting core growth channels by combining quick expense reductions with targeted revenue and margin initiatives.”
- Plan (90-day priorities): “(1) Confirm runway math and working capital, (2) implement hiring and discretionary spend controls, (3) secure vendor savings, (4) run manufacturing efficiency pilots, (5) test incremental price adjustments and high-margin product pushes.”
- Ask: “Approval to execute the 90‑day plan and permission to reallocate $X for a targeted automation pilot (if required). We’ll report weekly cash and operational KPIs and present modeled scenarios in two weeks.”

6) Simple scenario sensitivities (illustrative)
- Status quo: Burn = $240k → runway ≈ 8.8 months.
- Reduce expenses by 8.7% (save $90k/month): burn → $150k → runway = 14 months.
